{"status": "ok", "slug": "pr-300", "run_id": "41100699321-1", "run_dir": ".prflow/tmp/review/pr-300/41100699321-1", "diff_path": ".prflow/tmp/review/pr-300/41100699321-1/diff.patch", "mode": "pr", "base": "e22cc02a43f7ebd3ee8984c05e2926d6bba6e791", "base_sha": "e22cc02a43f7ebd3ee8984c05e2926d6bba6e791", "head_sha": "7e44e75bdbfa136c464061c966aa506d185e9e3f", "sections": {"rows": 13, "typechange": 0, "raw": 13, "logs": 0, "published": 13}, "files": [{"s": "A", "p": "changelog.d/300.fixed.md", "a": 6, "d": 0}, {"s": "M", "p": "docs/internal/mcp-server/transport.md", "a": 13, "d": 0}, {"s": "M", "p": "docs/internal/setup/preflight.md", "a": 1, "d": 1}, {"s": "M", "p": "src/sqllens/agent/integrations/anthropic/llm.py", "a": 10, "d": 6}, {"s": "M", "p": "src/sqllens/agent/integrations/mysql/sql_runner.py", "a": 11, "d": 3}, {"s": "M", "p": "src/sqllens/agent/integrations/postgres/sql_runner.py", "a": 11, "d": 3}, {"s": "A", "p": "src/sqllens/agent/integrations/sql_threads.py", "a": 46, "d": 0}, {"s": "M", "p": "src/sqllens/agent/integrations/sqlite/sql_runner.py", "a": 10, "d": 2}, {"s": "M", "p": "src/sqllens/preflight.py", "a": 1, "d": 1}, {"s": "A", "p": "tests/integration/test_slow_agent_run_responsiveness.py", "a": 180, "d": 0}, {"s": "M", "p": "tests/unit/test_llm_sampling_options.py", "a": 10, "d": 5}, {"s": "M", "p": "tests/unit/test_opus_history.py", "a": 39, "d": 7}, {"s": "A", "p": "tests/unit/test_sql_runner_event_loop.py", "a": 219, "d": 0}], "file_count": 13, "changed_lines": 585, "phase1_work_dir": ".prflow/tmp/review/pr-300/41100699321-1/phase1-b640434ea9836661", "batches": [{"k": 1, "first": 1, "last": 13, "slice": ".prflow/tmp/review/pr-300/41100699321-1/diff.patch"}], "flags": {"small_diff": false, "config_only": false, "has_new_types": true, "test_relevant": true}, "audit_hints": [{"file": "docs/internal/mcp-server/transport.md", "line": 112, "text": "`run(cfg)` starts one uvicorn process with one event loop, and `/healthz`, `/readyz`, every MCP session and every tool call share it. `/healthz` does no work of"}, {"file": "docs/internal/mcp-server/transport.md", "line": 114, "text": "- **Model calls.** `AnthropicLlmService` ([src/sqllens/agent/integrations/anthropic/llm.py](../../../src/sqllens/agent/integrations/anthropic/llm.py)) builds `a"}, {"file": "docs/internal/mcp-server/transport.md", "line": 115, "text": "- **SQL execution.** The SQLite, MySQL and Postgres runners' `run_sql` coroutines hand their synchronous driver work (`connect`, `execute`, `fetchmany`, `close`"}, {"file": "docs/internal/mcp-server/transport.md", "line": 121, "text": "Regression coverage: `tests/integration/test_slow_agent_run_responsiveness.py` holds a `query_database` model call open against a local stand-in for the Message"}, {"file": "tests/integration/test_slow_agent_run_responsiveness.py", "line": 6, "text": "An MCP client may call ``list_data_sources`` before each question, and a"}, {"file": "tests/integration/test_slow_agent_run_responsiveness.py", "line": 7, "text": "container health check polls ``/healthz`` every few seconds. Both are cheap,"}, {"file": "tests/integration/test_slow_agent_run_responsiveness.py", "line": 9, "text": "agent's model call blocks that loop, every other request waits until the"}, {"file": "tests/integration/test_slow_agent_run_responsiveness.py", "line": 51, "text": "\"stop_sequence\": None,"}, {"file": "tests/integration/test_slow_agent_run_responsiveness.py", "line": 57, "text": "start = {**_MESSAGE, \"content\": [], \"stop_reason\": None}"}, {"file": "tests/integration/test_slow_agent_run_responsiveness.py", "line": 65, "text": "{\"type\": \"message_delta\", \"delta\": {\"stop_reason\": \"end_turn\", \"stop_sequence\": None},"}, {"file": "tests/unit/test_opus_history.py", "line": 55, "text": "for block in final.content:"}, {"file": "tests/unit/test_opus_history.py", "line": 56, "text": "if block.type == \"text\":"}, {"file": "tests/unit/test_opus_history.py", "line": 60, "text": "def __init__(self) -> None:"}, {"file": "tests/unit/test_opus_history.py", "line": 66, "text": "async def __aexit__(self, *args: object) -> None:"}, {"file": "tests/unit/test_opus_history.py", "line": 152, "text": "assert [(call.name, call.arguments) for call in response.tool_calls or []] == ["}, {"file": "tests/unit/test_sql_runner_event_loop.py", "line": 6, "text": "The database drivers (``sqlite3``, PyMySQL, psycopg2) are synchronous. Each"}, {"file": "tests/unit/test_sql_runner_event_loop.py", "line": 8, "text": "would freeze every other request the server handles until the query returned."}, {"file": "tests/unit/test_sql_runner_event_loop.py", "line": 9, "text": "The runner tests make the driver deliberately slow and count how often a concurrent"}, {"file": "tests/unit/test_sql_runner_event_loop.py", "line": 39, "text": "async def heartbeat() -> None:"}, {"file": "tests/unit/test_sql_runner_event_loop.py", "line": 62, "text": ") -> None:"}, {"file": "tests/unit/test_sql_runner_event_loop.py", "line": 124, "text": "\"\"\"Occupy every SQL worker thread until ``release`` is set.\"\"\""}], "audit_hints_truncated": false, "views": {"head": {"dir": ".prflow/tmp/review/pr-300/41100699321-1/view-head", "revision": "7e44e75bdbfa136c464061c966aa506d185e9e3f"}, "base": {"dir": ".prflow/tmp/review/pr-300/41100699321-1/view-base", "revision": "e22cc02a43f7ebd3ee8984c05e2926d6bba6e791"}}, "pr": {"number": "300", "body": ".prflow/tmp/review/pr-300/41100699321-1/pr-body.md", "head_ref": "fix/issue-299-unblock-event-loop", "base_ref": "main", "api_head_sha": "7e44e75bdbfa136c464061c966aa506d185e9e3f", "author_trust": "not-looked-up"}, "issue": {"number": "299", "source": "pr-body", "context": ".prflow/tmp/review/pr-300/41100699321-1/issue-context.md"}, "warnings": []}
